ngs  because you cannot find these anywhere  else I would definitely grab the higher  editions but if you don't want to grab  any of those and you just want to play  the game the $30 Edition is there for  you now this game is very interesting  because it's a Buy to play MMO and RTS  hybrid it's very confusing in a sense  when you first think of it but as soon  as you start the game it gets a little  bit better MMO just like your standard  MMO titles with some RTS battles which  we'll get into later in the video and  showcase the game currently has five  playable classes being gunslinger spell  sword berserker Ranger and elementalist  each being gender locked at the moment  the game also has loads of different  troops like sorcerers orcs bowmen  mortarmen and a bunch of different  things like wizards and anything that  you can really think of  we're  - what those troops are like I said  later in the video but just to let you  know there's a loads of different things  to add to your army I ended up playing  as all five characters to really  understand what kind of abilities  they're getting but you'll for majority  of the gameplay you'll be seeing this  spell sword 1 because it's actually one  of my favorite characters and you know  for the easy thumbnail the character  creation for this game is one of the  more advanced things that I've seen in a  very long time with the recent mmo's  what you're going to be seeing is a lot  of previews in the bottom left as well  as a background cover to kind of  understand what the lighting looks like  for the character the preview isn't  going to be your default armor but  essentially saying hey this is the low  tier armor the mid tier and the endgame  armor and what it kind of looks like  with the character you can of course  change the hair color the eye color the  skin tone the lip color even go as far  as changing the actual face  reconstruction the hair style the color  of that decorations like tattoos or  piercings or anything like that on the  face or if you don't really know what to  do with your character or maybe you just  want to test out the character and don't  really feel like doing customization you  can go in the top left for the presets  and then we'll give you a whole new  character or if you have the basic stuff  down but just want to customize the  facial reconstruction and the bottom  right it has a random which is going to  randomize the face shape the eyes or  anything that has to do at the face  after creating your character the game  prompts you if you want to choose the  tutorial or not if this is are your 2nd  3rd 4th 5th character then obviously you  probably don't want to do the tutorial  but obviously on your first character  you definitely want to see the  understanding the game and the game is a  very good way of explaining what the  basics of how this game operates is you  could see from the game point that this  gives me a weird dynasty warriors feel  weird this giant person going up against  loads of different enemies killing like  18 to 20 of them at a time which I  personally love it gives it a really  nice feel of the war and it actually  feels like a giant war going on and not  just five people fighting five different  people there's actually large-scale  combat with hundreds and hundreds of  troops fighting at one time one thing I  do have to appreciate though is how  insane these cutscenes are one of the  things I definitely noticed is that I  actually really wasn't skipping  cutscenes even on multiple characters  because about the cool these things look  obviously they're not mocap 20:19  graphics where they look absolutely  real-life but for an MMO like this it  actually looks and astonishing the other  thing I must praise about this game is  how minimalistic the HUD is one of the  problems I had with PC and the Mo's is  that there's so much going on with the  amount of abilities and types of quests  that are happening is that because of  that there's so much happening on your  screen and it gets very claustrophobic  but the  game does a very good job of minimizing  how much is on screen by not giving you  exactly every single detail but  paraphrasing some things like on the  quests and showing you different icons  so that you know what you're doing  without having to be claustrophobic on  your screen now each character when you  hop into the game is going to have  multiple different menus you got your  inventory your skills your backpack your  map everything like that is going to be  there as well as the store which you can  of course purchase and things with  diamonds sometimes you don't have to you  of course don't have to buy the diamonds  yourself that's going to cost real world  money so if you don't want to do that  you totally don't have to but one thing  I noticed is that there's a mastery list  a skill list and a combo list and the  combo list had actually piqued my  interest because certain attacks can  actually combo into others and depending  on which way you use them you can  actually have different types of moves  for example one of the moves is just  tapping left-click that's your basic  attack well if you end up on locking  this part in the combo list you can  actually do left click then right click  afterwards to do a small little to hit  combo it's nothing crazy but it's a lot  better than constantly pressing one  button though all the time and button  mashing cuz that gets boring after a  while the quests are what you would  typically find in an MMO where they're  going to be small sometimes meaningless  quests were oh go kill this enemy go  light this fire go pick up these things  they're all gonna give you XP of course  but the real stuff is going to be the  dungeons which we'll talk about in a  little bit after we discussed the  individual characters the first  character is the gunslinger he's gonna  be your main attacker main dps type  character he doesn't have the most  amount of health but he's definitely  your all-around good character and  especially a very good beginner  character if you want to learn the ropes  of how to play Kingdom under fire - he  wields a sword and a pistol in the  second hand with a bunch of abilities  that either let you go from sword to gun  or just use the gun straight up and you  can use art to reload the gun it's  actually really cool and a lot of  different abilities that flow together  with the character your spell sword is  going to be your mage of the game she  has a bunch of things channeling the  magic of ice and lightning and using  those runes to go back and forth and  doing a bunch of elemental damage when  executed correctly she has these really  powerful runes that can actually rehear  yourself and that the reason they have  that is because she actually has a very  small health pool so she can keep  herself afloat so if you need somebody  that needs to just survive she's also  one of those characters speaking of  characters survive  we have the main take of the game the  Berserker this absolutely beefy looking  guy is definitely the biggest character  I've ever seen in a while  he is definitely your tank he is super  good at attacking multiple enemies at  the same exact time with his large  sweeping attacks and his giant sword you  can combine sword attacks with the  powerful core of rage in your hand doing  multiple different moves like slashing  sideways and then lifting the sword up  while using the rampage rune and a bunch  of other things in viewing your weapon  with dark energy and a bunch of  different things like I said to keep the  enemies focused on you and away from  your team the Rangers up next I find her  very opposite of the Berserker she has  very quick ranged and melee combat  attacks the problem is that while  inflicting very high damage just like  the Berserker she lacks the ability to  do a lot of damage when confronted by a  huge team of opponents so with the  Berserker he's really good at multiple  opponents whereas the Rangers were the  good at single target and the  elementalist  is a very skilled and versatile maid she  can use a bunch of things Dee buffing  and buffing opponents buffing your team  to give you more attack while also Dee  buffing the enemy team to give them less  defense and if that's not enough I like  to call the Beast masters because she  can use her magic to summon a bunch of  different companions to fight alongside  her one of the first ones you get is a  giant bear now we got to talk about the  real-time strategy within this game  especially within the one dungeon that  you first get at level 4 as the  commander of the army you have three  different options you have the C the X  and the Z key the C key is basically all  of your units follow you the x key is  the defense and the z key is your main  offense you can use the F keys at the  very top like f1 and f2 to go in between  different types of troops and selector  and unique abilities for example if you  highlight the archer troop you can  actually give them a damage boost to  their archery making them do a lot more  damage to flying targets or any big  targets that happen to be in your way  and towards the end of the dungeon  there's this huge large-scale fight  which looks absolutely insane after  after you've been using all of your  abilities and it's just really crazy how  having you can have a bunch of archers  in the back firing at the big scorpion  have a small little troop follow you to  the left with the other people staying  on defense towards the line protecting  the archers it's this huge strategy game  as well as being an MMO Alem one that  was basically the general overview of  the game Kingdom under fire - like I  said this game is available right now at  the time of this video is going  so if you do have a PC you definitely  want to play this game then difficult  click the link in the description down  below you can use that link to go get  the game as well as guys like to view if  you do enjoy subscribe if you're new  think you'd gain Forge for sponsoring  this video and peace out guys have a  great astir day goodbye  [Music]  [Music]

